  "notes": "Modified cash basis city; recorded as cash. Governmental data from governmental funds statement (p4), Total Governmental Funds column. Beginning/ending cash = beginning/ending fund balance (4,576,981 / 4,617,721), which includes certificates of deposit and county treasurer cash. Transfers: total column prints '-'; gross in 330,000 (Street 150,000, Fire 90,000, Other 90,000) and out 330,000 (General) from p4. Taxes line split using the statement of activities general receipts (p2): six lines sum to 1,204,965, 1 over printed 1,204,964. Re-check 2026-10-28: the property tax credit part of the Taxes split is now category Property Tax Credit and the in lieu tax part In Lieu of Tax (user rules). The p4 Intergovernmental 696,242 plus Grants and donations 398,146 correspond on p2 to operating grants 695,476 + state aid and equalization 180,034 + NPPD payments 218,879, but the report prints no breakdown of the Intergovernmental line itself, so it is not split. Business-type uses the cash-basis statement of activities (p2): beginning 2,041,350 (= cash 1,441,350 + CDs 600,000), ending 2,068,498 (= balance sheet p1); receipts = water/sewer charges (category Utility Charges, verifier fix 2026-10-28) plus general receipts (interest 38,078, gain on debt extinguishment 32,550); disbursements 772,532. Balance sheet (re-check 2026-10-28, user rule): governmental lines from the Balance Sheet - Modified Cash Basis - Governmental Funds (p3, Total Governmental Funds; 4,617,721 equals the government-wide governmental column on p1), fund balance by classification; business-type lines from the Statement of Net Position (p1); printed totals are the p1 Total column; no liabilities. Detail (verifier fix 2026-10-28, user rule 2026-10-27 per-fund detail): the only supplementary schedule (p8 Budgetary Comparison Schedule) is a combined all-funds schedule with fund totals only, so its lines were removed and detail is one line per fund column of the governmental funds statement (p4: General, Debt Service, Street, Fire, Other Governmental Funds; Total column not used) and of the business-type Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Net Position (p6, accrual: Water, Sewer; Total column not used). Per-fund Taxes lines kept as taxes (unlabeled) because the tax-type breakdown is printed only for all funds (p2). p6 nonoperating lines (interest income, gain on debt extinguishment, interest expense, loan fees) are outside the operating totals. The p8 schedule has 1-dollar rounding differences from p2 (investment earnings 38,079 vs 38,078; disbursements excluding transfers 3,319,213 vs 3,319,212). Read pages 1-8 of 8"
}
